{"id":"chatcmpl-a79e0a7e-ae11-4ce3-bc1d-336d31d03901","object":"chat.completion","created":1795229434,"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","reasoning_content":"","content":"{\n  \"highlights\": \"When interpreting lateral medical images with ambiguous laterality, use anatomical landmarks and expected normal asymmetries to infer the side of a finding. Absence of characteristic gas patterns (e.g., gastric bubble) under an elevated structure suggests a solid organ (e.g., liver) beneath, indicating the right side. Combine projection metadata with visual cues to resolve side-specific diagnoses.\",\n  \"patterns\": [\n    \"Use known normal anatomical asymmetries (e.g., right hemidiaphragm normally higher due to liver) to infer laterality when direct markers are absent.\",\n    \"Look for characteristic gas or fluid patterns (e.g., gastric bubble) to identify which side a structure belongs to; absence suggests solid organ underneath.\",\n    \"Leverage projection metadata (e.g., 'LT LAT') to constrain possible orientations and guide side determination.\",\n    \"When laterality is ambiguous, reason from statistical prevalence of isolated findings (e.g., right diaphragm elevation more commonly noted) as a tiebreaker.\"\n  ],\n  \"playbooks\": {\n    \"Radiology\": \"Use anatomical landmarks and expected normal asymmetries to infer laterality; check for gas patterns to distinguish left vs right; combine with projection labels.\",\n    \"Medical Imaging Interpretation\": \"When side is unclear, look for organ-specific signatures (gas, solid density) and use normal anatomical relationships as priors.\",\n    \"Visual Question Answering with Ambiguous Orientation\": \"Extract orientation cues from metadata and visual features; apply domain knowledge of normal asymmetries to resolve ambiguity.\"\n  },\n  \"checklists\": [\n    \"Confirm presence/absence of subdiaphragmatic gas (gastric bubble) to infer left vs right side.\",\n    \"Cross-check projection label (e.g., LT LAT) with visual landmarks to constrain orientation.\"\n  ]\n}"},"finish_reason":"stop","logprobs":null}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":1230,"total_tokens":1597,"completion_tokens":367,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"image_tokens":0,"text_tokens":1230},"completion_tokens_details":{"text_tokens":367}}}